<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 17 July, from 1402 to 1996.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/yongle-emperor" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yongle-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1402">1402 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">624 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Zhu Di takes the Ming throne as the Yongle Emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Zhu Di, fourth son of the dynasty's founder, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hongwu-emperor">Hongwu Emperor</a>, became the third Ming emperor, having seized the throne from his nephew. He later moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> and began building the Forbidden City.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yongle-emperor">Yongle Emperor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1429">1429 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">597 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles VII is crowned king of France at Reims</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Charles VII, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> since 1422, was crowned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reims">Reims</a> Cathedral, the traditional place of French coronations, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a> had raised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-orleans">siege of Orléans</a>. He went on to recover northern France and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a> from the English.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-vii-of-france">Charles VII of France</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1453">1453 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">573 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">French artillery wins the Battle of Castillon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a> cut down an English army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-talbot-1st-earl-of-shrewsbury">John Talbot</a> at Castillon in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a>. It was the last battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>, leaving Calais as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>'s only possession in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1762">1762 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">264 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Deposed Tsar Peter III dies in captivity</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Days after his wife Catherine seized the throne in a coup, Peter III died at Ropsha, almost certainly murdered by her supporters. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine the Great</a> went on to rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> for 34 years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine the Great</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bolsheviks execute the Romanov family in Yekaterinburg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the early hours, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a>, his wife, their five children and four retainers were shot in the cellar of the Ipatiev House. Their remains were found decades later; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox Church</a> canonised the family in 2000.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Potsdam Conference opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Truman, Stalin and Churchill, later replaced by Attlee, met at Cecilienhof near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>. They settled the occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and issued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potsdam-declaration">Potsdam Declaration</a> demanding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s unconditional surrender.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1975">1975 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">51 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">American and Soviet spacecraft dock in orbit</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> capsule docked with Soyuz 19, and Thomas <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stafford">Stafford</a> and Alexei Leonov shook hands through the hatch. The first international crewed space mission was a landmark of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> détente.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1996">1996 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">30 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">TWA Flight 800 explodes off Long Island</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Boeing 747 bound for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> exploded minutes after take-off from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, killing all 230 on board. Investigators concluded that a spark had ignited fuel vapour in the centre wing tank.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li></ol>
